{"lines": ["In July 1909, the brand-new liner Waratah left Durban, South Africa, for Cape Town with 211 people on board.", "Newspapers called her \"practically immune from any danger of sinking.\"", "She had no radio.", "One passenger, Claude Sawyer, got off at Durban, even though his ticket went on to Cape Town.", "He worried the ship rolled too much, and later told an inquiry he'd had frightening dreams.", "Early next morning, the freighter Clan MacIntyre swapped lamp signals with her, and logged it.", "A few hours later, she dropped over the horizon, her last confirmed sighting.", "Then the weather turned into a violent storm, and she never reached Cape Town.", "Search ships found nothing.", "In 1999, sonar found a wreck that seemed to match, but it was another ship.", "No wreckage of the Waratah has ever been found.", "And nine years later, the sea did it again, this time to a Navy ship with 306 people aboard."], "words": [["In", 0.0, 0.1], ["July", 0.1, 0.3], ["1909,", 0.3, 0.98], ["the", 2.12, 2.3], ["brand-new", 2.3, 2.8], ["liner", 2.8, 3.06], ["Waratah", 3.06, 3.64], ["left", 3.64, 3.94], ["Durban,", 3.94, 4.46], ["South", 4.72, 4.98], ["Africa,", 4.98, 5.42], ["for", 5.94, 6.06], ["Cape", 6.06, 6.22], ["Town", 6.22, 6.58], ["with", 6.58, 7.14], ["211", 7.14, 7.48], ["people", 7.48, 8.76], ["on", 8.76, 8.96], ["board.", 8.96, 9.28], ["Newspapers", 9.9, 10.34], ["called", 10.34, 10.76], ["her", 10.76, 11.02], ["\"practically", 11.32, 11.68], ["immune", 11.68, 12.06], ["from", 12.06, 12.54], ["any", 12.54, 12.68], ["danger", 12.68, 13.16], ["of", 13.16, 13.36], ["sinking.\"", 13.36, 13.58], ["She", 14.22, 14.38], ["had", 14.38, 14.52], ["no", 14.52, 14.8], ["radio.", 14.8, 15.2], ["One", 15.92, 16.06], ["passenger,", 16.06, 16.56], ["Claude", 17.02, 17.28], ["Sawyer,", 17.28, 17.62], ["got", 18.08, 18.24], ["off", 18.24, 18.46], ["at", 18.46, 18.58], ["Durban,", 18.58, 19.04], ["even", 19.4, 19.7], ["though", 19.7, 19.9], ["his", 19.9, 20.08], ["ticket", 20.0